# MCP demo: the same program with one deliberate syntax error (a dangling `&&`)
"""
# Validated records over MCP (broken on purpose)

The same program as `validated_records.genia` with one deliberate syntax error, used to show
`genia_parse` diagnostics. It does not parse; the repaired program is `validated_records.genia`.

## Run

Submit this file's source to `genia_parse` through an MCP client (see `docs/mcp/demo.md`) to see
the diagnostic. Directly, it fails with a syntax error:

```bash
genia examples/mcp/validated_records_broken.genia
```

## Features Demonstrated

* a structured parse diagnostic (a character offset) from `genia_parse`
* the repair loop: parse, read the diagnostic, fix, parse again
"""

records = [
  {id: 1, name: "Ada", age: 36},
  {id: 2, name: "Grace"},
  {id: 3, name: "Alan", age: -4},
  {id: 4, name: "Edsger", age: 72}
]

valid_age(age) = age >= 0 &&

check(record) =
  validate_record(record, {
    id: (r) -> validate_required("id", r),
    name: (r) -> validate_required("name", r),
    age: (r) -> validate_field("age", valid_age, "age between 0 and 150", r)
  })

report = records |> ((items) -> validate_each(items, check)) |> collect_validated

print(length(report.clean))
report.diagnostics |> each((d) -> writeln(stderr, diagnostic_reason(d))) |> run
report
